# src/tychoc.c:9128 -- the base being indexed must itself be a place, and
# `rows[0]` is a string element of a SCALAR array, which is not. Pinned since
# compiler/types/tcheck.ty@_is_lvalue made tychoc1's place test type-aware too.
# expect: cannot index-assign through this expression (only a variable, field, composite-array element, or map value is a place)
fn main():
    rows := ["ab", "cd"]
    rows[0][1] = 'z'
    println(rows[0])
